tion?","codeSnippet":null,"codeLanguage":null,"type":"MultipleChoice","allowsMultipleAnswers":false,"options":[{"id":"7da0e471-4ad3-4abb-be3c-c92758054d03","text":"Tabulation is top-down recursion with a cache","displayOrder":0},{"id":"042d6069-25c8-4039-8baa-c512052fef1d","text":"Tabulation fills a table bottom-up iteratively; memoisation caches results of top-down recursive calls","displayOrder":1},{"id":"f5cdb14b-2bce-4879-8a1e-ad664e5a8d48","text":"Only memoisation is DP","displayOrder":2},{"id":"e72a2c10-a5bf-4361-a925-95bcfae0eb7f","text":"Tabulation always uses less memory","displayOrder":3}],"points":1.0000,"selectedOptionIds":[],"isMarkedForReview":false},{"questionId":"a0b35d8d-34b5-4b02-9894-c31afdc18630","order":4,"title":"Why String is immutable","body":"Which is a benefit of `String` being immutable in Java?","codeSnippet":null,"codeLanguage":null,"type":"MultipleChoice","allowsMultipleAnswers":false,"options":[{"id":"da270044-d606-4f60-8c31-14fbe00a1ee3","text":"Strings can be modified in place faster","displayOrder":0},{"id":"19601dd2-ac24-4b8d-ae98-d9dd9fc09df8","text":"Strings can be safely shared, cached (string pool) and used as HashMap keys and across threads","displayOrder":1},{"id":"382efd73-a4b0-4e12-a83d-3b17544ea7cd","text":"It uses less memory when concatenating in loops","displayOrder":2},{"id":"806f1dc4-0c92-4a7e-a940-d823f8053330","text":"It disables garbage collection","displayOrder":3}],"points":1.0000,"selectedOptionIds":[],"isMarkedForReview":false},{"questionId":"d78a6405-479a-47f3-b9c2-b55495692809","order":5,"title":"Discriminated unions","body":"Given `type Shape = { kind: 'circle'; r: number } | { kind: 'square'; side: number }`, how does TypeScript know `shape.r` exists inside `if (shape.kind === 'circle')`?","codeSnippet":null,"codeLanguage":null,"type":"MultipleChoice","allowsMultipleAnswers":false,"options":[{"id":"4ee996ce-f051-498e-80d6-707d6fe78b1a","text":"It doesn't; you must cast","displayOrder":0},{"id":"c5b45313-4956-4053-bb88-9a2f2fbaa606","text":"Checking the literal discriminant property narrows the union to the matching member","displayOrder":1},{"id":"0cffd65d-6314-47a9-b5d8-e349eedba156","text":"Because r is declared first","displayOrder":2},{"id":"56eafc88-5315-47fe-abef-829d51f0c285","text":"Runtime reflection","displayOrder":3}],"points":1.0000,"selectedOptionIds":[],"isMarkedForReview":false},{"questionId":"eb6c39cf-d510-4133-8697-e58c0df02299","order":6,"title":"Mutable default arguments","body":"What does this print?","codeSnippet":"def add(item, items=[]):\n    items.append(item)\n    return items\n\nadd(1)\nprint(add(2))","codeLanguage":"python","type":"MultipleChoice","allowsMultipleAnswers":false,"options":[{"id":"8b5507de-d7f1-4fac-88fb-ea3014bbac2e","text":"[2]","displayOrder":0},{"id":"56b90adb-339f-4f81-8f64-c26f1c4fa577","text":"[1, 2]","displayOrder":1},{"id":"a69297a9-bff4-4f5f-984b-272babdf30a1","text":"[]","displayOrder":2},{"id":"762d8ea4-c1cd-48f0-8fa9-17e0909ac601","text":"It raises TypeError","displayOrder":3}],"points":1.0000,"selectedOptionIds":[],"isMarkedForReview":false},{"questionId":"3272f642-c1c5-4675-b55d-f832e9149eab","order":7,"title":"GC and Dispose","body":"True or false: the garbage collector automatically calls `Dispose()` on unreachable objects that implement `IDisposable`.","codeSnippet":null,"codeLanguage":null,"type":"TrueFalse","allowsMultipleAnswers":false,"options":[{"id":"a387b3b1-4d9a-4bc7-9a83-5414195e657c","text":"True","displayOrder":0},{"id":"b14c74ae-3d57-4064-9d4b-56f5bc402d2d","text":"False","displayOrder":1}],"points":1.0000,"selectedOptionIds":[],"isMarkedForReview":false},{"questionId":"858f4a5e-9920-42ea-a3cb-0159c65daeb9","order":8,"title":"Authentication before authorization","body":"Why must `UseAuthentication()` be placed before `UseAuthorization()`?","codeSnippet":null,"codeLanguage":null,"type":"MultipleChoice","allowsMultipleAnswers":false,"options":[{"id":"1d87c5dc-1395-4d5b-8dd4-10e6f5491412","text":"It is just a convention with no effect","displayOrder":0},{"id":"a1409744-ecd5-44e5-bbd1-314e12f7fefb","text":"Authorization evaluates HttpContext.User, which authentication middleware populates from the request credentials","displayOrder":1},{"id":"103f51b4-df34-4a31-b323-81f6523aacaf","text":"Authorization middleware starts the authentication handlers itself","displayOrder":2},{"id":"f8728b88-c9e7-4dbf-b251-de8dac5f01da","text":"Because UseAuthorization registers the JWT handler","displayOrder":3}],"points":1.0000,"selectedOptionIds":[],"isMarkedForReview":false},{"questionId":"18dcd19e-cbee-43cb-a814-13799e6afec5","order":9,"title":"Quicksort worst case","body":"What is quicksort's worst-case time complexity and when does it occur?","codeSnippet":null,"codeLanguage":null,"type":"MultipleChoice","allowsMultipleAnswers":false,"options":[{"id":"00695695-629b-4a2d-9640-87136d35fddb","text":"O(n log n), never worse","displayOrder":0},{"id":"a71b55ca-92d4-425e-b376-d263019f84fc","text":"O(n²), when pivots repeatedly split the array very unevenly (e.g. first-element pivot on sorted input)","displayOrder":1},{"id":"57d3626b-505e-425a-8625-8f6bf489d85c","text":"O(n), on sorted input","displayOrder":2},{"id":"5c4aa514-2ecf-433c-9ec5-e7824cf8448a","text":"O(log n)","displayOrder":3}],"points":1.0000,"selectedOptionIds":[],"isMarkedForReview":false},{"questionId":"94cba40b-74ea-4659-8759-9c1538a0f635","order":10,"title":"The GIL","body":"In standard CPython builds, what does the Global Interpreter Lock imply for CPU-bound code?","codeSnippet":null,"codeLanguage":null,"type":"MultipleChoice","allowsMultipleAnswers":false,"options":[{"id":"dabe0415-a161-4402-987c-5ee9a73b3933","text":"Threads run Python bytecode truly in parallel on all cores","displayOrder":0},{"id":"32ddcb16-5378-4a79-845a-3ae9f7210854","text":"Only one thread executes Python bytecode at a time, so CPU-bound work should use multiprocessing (or native extensions)","displayOrder":1},{"id":"2f2f6a28-70c6-4516-9639-